The '''Imperial Inspectorate HQ''', also known as the '''Imperial Inspectorate Command Center''', was the headquarters of the [[Inspectorate]]. Located on the [[Core Worlds|Core World]] [[Coruscant]], it was originally a [[Republic Military]] facility, known as the '''Republic Center for Military Operations''' or the '''Republic military base''', during the final [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. The [[architect]] who designed the base was [[Lieutenant Commander]] [[Orson Callan Krennic]]. It later became the '''Naval Intelligence Headquarters''', or '''Naval Intelligence Agency building''', as the headquarters of [[Imperial Military]]'s [[Naval Intelligence Agency]].

During the [[Clone Wars]], former [[Jedi Commander]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] was trained by clones and was also put on [[Trial of Ahsoka Tano|trial]] for [[treason]] at the Republic Center for Military Operations. The charges against Tano were dropped after another [[Jedi]], [[Commander]] [[Barriss Offee]], was revealed as the true culprit behind the [[terrorist]] [[Bombing of the Jedi Temple hangar|bombing]] of the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]].

With the [[Imperial Era|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], the Republic Center for Military Operations was re-designated as the Imperial Inspectorate HQ. It formed the so-called "supreme triangle" in [[Imperial City]]'s [[Federal District]], together with the [[Imperial Palace]] and the [[COMPNOR arcology]].

==Description==
{{Quote|You don't have to tell me any more, Commander Tano.''"<br />"''I don't?''"<br />"''No. There are recorders in every room. Curiously, the sound isn't working on this one.|Wilhuff Tarkin and Ahsoka Tano|<ref name="Knew Too Much" />}}
[[File:ImperialInspectorateHQ-2016DoctorAphra15.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The Imperial Inspectorate HQ was originally a Republic military base during the Clone Wars.]]
The [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Inspectorate]] HQ was a [[deflector shield|shielded]], hardened, near-windowless complex<ref name="Tarkin" /> located on the [[capital]] [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]'s [[Federal District]], alongside the [[COMPNOR arcology]] and the [[Imperial Palace]] itself. The complex was located adjacent to the [[Coruscant shipyard]]s<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-jedi-who-knew-too-much-trivia-gallery|text="The Jedi Who Knew Too Much" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> where [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyers]] docked.<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref>

[[File:CrosshairAtImperialInspectorateCafeteria.png|thumb|250x250px|Inspectorate HQ's cafeteria]]
The Inspectorate possessed [[scanner]], [[sensor]], and [[communications array]]s on its roof during the [[Imperial Era]] and was defended by two [[turbolaser]] batteries. It also had micro-[[Holocamera|holocams]]<ref name="Tarkin" /> and [[recorder]]s built in every corner of the complex<ref name="Knew Too Much" /> so that the actions and conversations of every worker could be monitored.<ref name="Tarkin" /> Several enclosed [[hangar]]s<ref name="PMP">{{TOTJ|Practice Makes Perfect (episode)}}</ref> and landing bays were scattered in the grounds around the facility and hosted multiple [[transport]]s and [[starfighter]]s.<ref name="Knew Too Much" /> The base was also home to the military [[prison]] which hosted high-profile Separatists too valuable to send to a criminal incarceration facility, including [[Emir]] [[Wat Tambor]], [[Archduke]] [[Poggle the Lesser]] and [[General]] [[Whorm Loathsom]].<ref name="Trivia" /> The prison also hosted former [[Jedi]] [[Barriss Offee]], convicted of treason after the [[Bombing of the Jedi Temple hangar|bombing of the Jedi Temple Hangar]].<ref name="Empire">{{TOTE|Devoted}}</ref>

The [[Strategic Planning Amphitheater]] was located at the summit of the facility.<ref name="Catalyst" /> The [[First Battle Memorial]]<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=explore/the-clone-wars/ep518|text="The Jedi Who Knew Too Much" - ''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide|nolive=1}}</ref> was built in the center of the base's plaza, its purpose to honor the [[clone trooper]]s that were [[Death|killed]] in the [[First Battle of Geonosis]]. This commemorative monument was constructed on an enormous slab of [[Color|reddish-brown]] rock, taken from the [[planet]] [[Geonosis]] and made into a wall engraved with the designations of the fallen [[Cloning|clones]].

==History==
===The Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Rex, call security. Tell them we need to search the entire base. Now!|Anakin Skywalker, to Captain [[Rex]]|<ref name="Knew Too Much" />}}
[[File:RepublicMilitaryBaseCourtyard-TWJ.png|thumb|250px|The Republic Center for Military Operations was constructed on Coruscant, the capital world of the Galactic Republic.|left]]
During the [[Republic Era|final years]] of the [[Galactic Republic]], the Republic Center for Military Operations was the base of operations and strategic center of the [[Republic Military]]. Remodeled and expanded by the [[architect]] [[Orson Callan Krennic]] of the [[Republic Corps of Engineers|Corps of Engineers]], it was located in the [[Federal District]] of [[Imperial City|Galactic City]] on the [[Core Worlds|Core World]] [[Coruscant]]&mdash;the [[Galaxy|galactic]] [[capital]] of the Republic&mdash;at the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Catalyst" /> As the Republic waged war against the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] across [[the galaxy]], the facility served as the operation hub<ref name="Knew Too Much Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-jedi-who-knew-too-much-episode-guide|text="The Jedi Who Knew Too Much" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]].<ref name="Tarkin" />

A committee of Republic officials, known as the [[Strategic Advisory Cell]], convened in the Republic Center's Strategic Planning Amphitheater to discuss plans for the creation of a Republic [[superweapon]] in the first [[Standard year|year]] of the Clone Wars.<ref name="Catalyst" /> At one point during the war, [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] recruited [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] and his men to help his [[Padawan]], [[Ahsoka Tano]], practice her lightsaber abilities at the base's hangar. The clones stood in a circle around Tano and fired on her with stun blasts as she practiced deflecting them. Skywalker pushed his apprentice to keep trying even as she was knocked unconscious several times.<ref name="PMP" /> As the conflict dragged on, one of the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple's]] [[starship]] [[hangar]]s was [[Bombing of the Jedi Temple hangar|bombed]] by [[terrorist]]s, resulting in the [[death]]s of several [[Jedi]], clone [[trooper]]s, and [[Technician|maintenance workers]]. A [[Coruscanti|local]], [[Letta Turmond]], was arrested by [[Jedi General]] Anakin Skywalker<ref name="Sabotage">{{TCW|Sabotage (episode)}}</ref> and [[Prison|imprisoned]] at the Republic military base due to her involvement in the attack against the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Knew Too Much" />

[[File:RepublicMiliaryCourtroom-TWJ.png|thumb|250px|The trial of Ahsoka Tano took place in the Republic Center for Military Operations.]]
Turmond was subsequently [[Force choke|killed by way of]] [[the Force]] while under interrogation by Skywalker's [[Padawan|apprentice]], [[Jedi Commander]] Ahsoka Tano. Accused of murder, Tano [[Escape from the Republic military base|escaped]] from the base and fled into hiding in the [[Coruscant Underworld|lower levels]] of Coruscant.<ref name="Knew Too Much" /> Pursued by the [[Imperial shock trooper|clone shock troopers]] of the [[Coruscant Guard]], Tano was eventually [[Capture of Ahsoka Tano|captured]]<ref name="TCAJ">{{TCW|To Catch a Jedi}}</ref> and taken back to the Republic Center for Military Operations where she faced a military tribunal presided over by [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]]. Before sentencing could be carried out, however, Skywalker [[Duel at the Jedi Temple|arrested]] Jedi [[Commander]] [[Barriss Offee]] after discovering that she was responsible for the bombing at the [[Jedi temple|Temple]] as well as the framing of Tano. He took the fallen Jedi to the base's courtroom where Offee confessed to her crimes against both the Republic and the Order. As a result, the tribunal acquitted Tano on all charges, although she declined to rejoin either the Jedi or the Grand [[Army]].<ref name="TWJ">{{TCW|The Wrong Jedi}}</ref> Wat Tambor later escaped from the detention center.<ref name="OSWM 121">{{GermanFanCite|121|Database}}</ref>

===The Imperial Era===
[[File:CaM_back_cover_art.png|thumb|left|250px|During the reign of the Galactic Empire, the Imperial Inspectorate HQ was infiltrated by Rebel Alliance operatives.]]
When the war ended<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> in [[19 BBY]],<ref name="19 BBY">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the [[Proclamation of the New Order|beginning]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] to [[19 BBY]].</ref> the Republic was [[Proclamation of the New Order|replaced]] by the Galactic Empire.<ref name="Episode III" /> As a result, the headquarters of the Imperial Inspectorate,<ref name="Aphra 15" /> as well as the [[Naval Intelligence Agency]], was constructed over the monads of the former Republic military base. Together with the Imperial Palace and the [[COMPNOR arcology]], the Imperial Inspectorate HQ was part of the "supreme triangle" in the Federal District.<ref name="Tarkin" />

A short time into the Imperial regime,<ref name="Bad Batch Date 2">{{TBBDate|203}}</ref> the clone [[Crosshair]] was assigned by [[Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart]] to a [[Crosshair and Cody's team|team]] of troopers that would be undertaking a [[Mission to Desix|infiltration mission]] to the planet [[Desix]]. After meeting the admiral in his [[Vice Admiral Rampart's office|office]] within Inspectorate HQ, Crosshair was instructed to meet with the unit's commander, [[Cody]], outside of the building near the First Battle Memorial.<ref name="The Solitary Clone" />

When the clone troopers were officially phased out of the [[Imperial Army]] and replaced by the [[human]] recruits of [[Project War-Mantle]], the clones were processed at the Inspectorate HQ before being sent into retirement.<ref name="Navy HQ">{{Databank|naval-intelligence-headquarters|Naval Intelligence Headquarters}}</ref>

In [[14 BBY]],<ref name="Date-Tarkin">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']] to [[14 BBY]].</ref> the headquarters served as the meeting place of [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] Palpatine, his [[Joint Chiefs of the Imperial Military|Joint Chiefs]] of the [[Imperial Military]], and leaders of the [[Commission for the Preservation of the New Order]], when a [[Berch Teller's rebel cell|group of rebels]] hijacked [[Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]]'s [[Carrion Spike|personal corvette]] and used it to go on a rampage throughout the Empire.<ref name="Tarkin" /> At one point during the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[agent]]s of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] infiltrated the complex.<ref name="Cypers and Masks">''[[Cyphers and Masks]]''</ref>

Around [[1 ABY]],<ref name="Date-Aphra">{{Aphra2016Date|15}}</ref> [[Lieutenant-Inspector]] [[Magna Tolvan]] went to the facility following her promotion to the agency, where she researched her deceased mentor, [[Thanoth]], with an [[RA-7 protocol droid]].<ref name="Aphra 15" /> Around [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Date-SW">The events of ''Star Wars'' 36 take place after the [[Escape from Cloud City]] and before the [[Rescue of Han Solo]], which are dated to [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]], respectively, by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''.</ref> when the Alliance made an [[Assault on Coruscant|attack run]] at Coruscant, an Imperial [[Unidentified Imperial lieutenant (Inspectorate)|lieutenant]] informed the [[Unidentified Imperial commander (Inspectorate)|commander]] of the Inspectorate headquarters of the impending attack. The commander ordered for the orbital platforms to be activated and called for half of the planetary-defense fighter wings to be scrambled. Following the rebels succeeding their attack, the commander and the lieutenant left Inspectorate HQ to see the damage caused to a statue of the Emperor.<ref name="Star Wars 36">[[Star Wars (2020) 36|''Star Wars'' (2020) 36]]</ref>

